# EXTERNAL authentication and Hello on a D-Bus bus with the stock system policy.
#
# Provenance: measured by the Lead for feature #34 (plan row 16) on dbus-daemon 1.14.10 of the development host with
# /usr/share/dbus-1/system.conf (only <listen> moved to a scratch path; <user>, <fork>, <pidfile>, <syslog> and the
# includes removed), a Python client run as uid 0 and as uid 65534 (setpriv); the daemon was stopped afterwards.
#
# Exchange: the client sends one NUL byte, "AUTH EXTERNAL <hex of the ASCII decimal uid>" and CR LF; the daemon
# answers the line below (the guid differs per daemon start) and CR LF. After "BEGIN" and Hello (serial 1) the daemon
# sends, in one write, the method return of Hello (flags NO_REPLY_EXPECTED, destination :1.1, reply_serial 1,
# signature s, sender org.freedesktop.DBus, body the unique name) and then a unicast NameAcquired signal to the new
# connection. The hex below is those two messages, 258 bytes, for uid 65534 and unique name :1.1.
